## Priority

Work top-down. Items in the same band are independent.

### Band 1 — blocks acceptance, needs protocol design

| # | Fix | Reviewer | Why first |
|---|---|---|---|
| **F1** | Bind `S_Q` to the authorized query | R3-1 | Authorization bypass. The most serious finding in the review set. Nothing else matters if this stands. |
| **F2** | Bind node policies `P_u` to record policies `P_i` | R3-2 | Same vulnerability class — node-level access silently grants record-level access |
| **F3** | TDAs verify query authorization before partial decryption | R3-3 | Completes F1; without it the authorities are a decryption oracle |
| **F4** | Instantiate ABSE concretely | R1-C2, R3-4, R3-5 | Every security theorem is conditional until this lands |

F1–F3 are one coherent change to the aggregation path. Design them together.

